{"parentUuid":"4e4e7f3e-230e-4e89-a771-9c1681cd6350","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-15","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"test/visual","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01qUyZaFhlkHRDI2oxD3oNBN","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Playwright puts the browser and the operating system into every snapshot's file name: on a Mac it writes moorings-table-chromium-darwin.png, and on the Linux CI runner it looks for moorings-table-chromium-linux.png. Only the darwin files are committed, so CI has nothing to compare against. That is on purpose in Playwright: the same page renders differently on each OS (fonts, font hinting, anti-aliasing), so a Mac screenshot would not match a Linux one pixel for pixel anyway.\n\nSo the Linux snapshots have to be produced on Linux, and the same Linux as CI, or they will drift again. The usual way is to run the tests in Playwright's own Docker image, with the same version as @playwright/test, both to update snapshots and in CI. Let me check the versions."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":743,"output_tokens":181}},"uuid":"df5d3bec-fccc-4576-ab11-d994f5390a26","timestamp":"2026-09-25T14:02:34.000Z","requestId":"req_011CEhwjbxxxJ4bNtLCwysMD"}
